    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOH2Qg5s7l6k_V",
      "title": "all: rename Interop hardfork to Lagoon",
      "author": "digorithm",
      "number": 803,
      "body": "## Summary\n\nThe Interop hardfork is being renamed to Lagoon across the OP Stack. This PR carries the op-geth side.\n\n- `params.ChainConfig.InteropTime` → `LagoonTime`, JSON tag `interopTime` → `lagoonTime`, `IsInterop` → `IsLagoon`. **Hard cut, no legacy alias** — no production chain has `interopTime` set in genesis, so the wire break is acceptable.\n- Bundled superchain mirror `HardforkConfig.InteropTime` → `LagoonTime` with TOML tag `interop_time` → `lagoon_time`.\n- Bumps embedded superchain-registry to [`ac4e485`](https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/superchain-registry/commit/ac4e48516794322e20abfe4f4c175e379b9a5d19) (post-rename, [SR #1255](https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/superchain-registry/pull/1255)), so the bundled TOMLs use `lagoon_time`.\n\nTracks ethereum-optimism/optimism#21135.\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- The `--override.interop` CLI flag is left unchanged to avoid breaking operator scripts. Internal Go symbol `OverrideOptimismInterop` is also unchanged.\n- Higher-level \"Interop\" feature naming (e.g. `CurrentInteropBlockTime`, `filterInteropTxs`) is unchanged — this PR scopes to fork-timestamp naming only.\n\n## Coordination\n\nThis PR is the upstream half of a coordinated rename. The monorepo PR that consumes this commit will go up next, with `replace github.com/ethereum/go-ethereum => ...` pointing at this branch for CI validation. Per workflow: monorepo PR validates against this branch first, then this PR merges, then the monorepo PR's pin is updated.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `go build ./...` — clean\n- [x] `go test ./params/... ./superchain/... ./eth/... ./core/... ./miner/...` — 31 packages, 0 failures\n- [ ] CI passes on this branch\n- [ ] Coordinated monorepo PR builds and tests green against this branch",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/op-geth",
      "createdAt": "2026-06-12T20:25:37Z",
      "mergedAt": null,
      "additions": 26,
      "deletions": 26
